 "final_text": "I have successfully implemented the Acyclic Visitor pattern in C++20 as requested. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Files Created/Modified:\n\n1. **include/acyclic.hpp** - The framework with:\n   - `struct VisitorBase`: polymorphic, empty marker\n   - `template <class T> struct Visitor`: abstract with virtual visit method\n   - `struct Trade`: abstract with accept, try_accept, and type_name methods\n   - `template <class Derived> struct VisitableTrade : Trade` (CRTP): implements accept/try_accept with dynamic_cast checking\n   - `class UnsupportedTrade`: inherits from std::runtime_error with type_name in what()\n\n2. **include/trades.hpp** - Library's own content:\n   - `struct Swap : VisitableTrade<Swap>` with type_name \"Swap\"\n   - `struct Bond : VisitableTrade<Bond>` with type_name \"Bond\"\n   - `class NotionalVisitor` compiled in src/trades.cpp with support for Swap and Bond trades\n\n3. **src/trades.cpp** - Library's own content:\n   - Implementation of Swap and Bond constructors\n\n## Key Features:\n\n- **Acyclic**: Third parties can add new trades and new visitors without editing or recompiling the library\n- **No coupling**: The base class doesn't know about concrete types\n- **Runtime type checking**: Uses dynamic_cast to determine if a visitor supports a trade type\n- **Proper error handling**: Throws UnsupportedTrade when a visitor doesn't support a trade type\n- **Try functionality**: Provides try_accept method that returns false instead of throwing\n\n## Verification:\n\nThe implementation was tested to ensure:\n- Existing trades (Swap, Bond) can be visited by NotionalVisitor\n- New trade types can be added by third parties without modifying the library\n- New visitors can be added by third parties without modifying the library\n- Unsupported trades properly throw UnsupportedTrade exceptions\n- try_accept returns false for unsupported trades instead of throwing\n\nThe implementation fully satisfies the requirements for an acyclic visitor pattern that allows third-party extensions without recompilation of the core library.",
